\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5 (claude-sonnet-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Warlpiri (ISO 639-3 wbp) is spoken in the Northern Territory, Australia. Contrary to the premise that it is not known to be taught, the search results show a long-running bilingual programme at Yuendumu and use as a language of instruction at Yuendumu and Nyirrpi schools.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Linguistic Innovation and Continuity: Teaching in and of Warlpiri Language at Yuendumu School (ANU repository): \url{https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/items/4370cec5-3e45-42eb-a317-9986d1c08945}
\item From Linguistic Research Findings to Useful Products for Australian Aboriginal Communities (\emph{eTropic}): \url{https://journals.jcu.edu.au/etropic/article/view/3395}
\item Same article, PDF: \url{https://journals.jcu.edu.au/index.php/etropic/article/download/3395/3335/6535}
\end{itemize}
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item \emph{Warlpiri Encyclopaedic Dictionary}, over 1,400 pages with English translations, examples, illustrations and a grammar guide: \url{https://shop.aiatsis.gov.au/products/warlpiri-encyclopaedic-dictionary}
\item AIATSIS news item on the dictionary: \url{https://aiatsis.gov.au/whats-new/news/cross-disciplinary-work-produces-landmark-warlpiri-dictionary}
\item Artshub coverage: \url{https://www.artshub.com.au/news/news/landmark-warlpiri-dictionary-puts-living-ancient-language-first-2607244/}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None specifically found. Over 210 Warlpiri speakers contributed to the dictionary.
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None specifically found; a search for Warlpiri Media returned nothing.
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Bilingual education began at Yuendumu in 1975. Yuendumu School aims for bilingual biliteracy, treating Warlpiri as both teaching medium and learning goal. Further school materials would need searching beyond what was found here.
\end{document}
